          "answer_excerpt": "# Technical Analysis of Plant Condition Records: Units 0000000\u20130000017\n\n## 1. Scope and Method\n\nThis report analyzes 18 condition-monitoring records drawn from heterogeneous asset classes (separators, scrubbers, pipelines, valves, reactors, pumps, and turbines) across stations in the network. Each record contains five measured parameters: pressure (kPa), temperature (\u00b0C), flow (m\u00b3/h), vibration velocity (mm/s RMS), and process efficiency (%).\n\nBecause the dataset mixes asset types with very different expected operating envelopes, the analysis proceeds in three stages:\n\n1. **Cross-asset triage** using vibration velocity and efficiency as the two universal indicators, since ISO 10816-style vibration limits and efficiency degradation apply meaningfully regardless of equipment class.\n2. **Asset-class-specific review**, where each unit is judged against plausible normal ranges for its type.\n3. **Failure-mode inference**, linking abnormal parameter combinations to credible root causes, followed by concrete maintenance actions.\n\nA note on methodology: with only one snapshot per unit, trend information is absent. All conclusions below are therefore *conditional* \u2014 they identify the most probable failure modes given the measurement pattern, and they prescribe the measurements needed to confirm or refute the diagnosis. Where a reading",
