          "finish_reason": "length",
          "answer_excerpt": "# Technical Analysis of Plant Equipment Records \u2014 Units at Stations 11\u2013360\n\n## 1. Executive Summary\n\nEighteen records spanning seven equipment classes (heat exchangers, turbines, condensers, separators, valves, scrubbers, pumps, and pipelines) were reviewed for condition-based maintenance planning. The dataset shows no single imminent catastrophic failure signature, but it does reveal a **systemic vibration problem**, a cluster of **heat-exchanger efficiency losses**, **pressure anomalies on two condensers**, and **one severe cold-side temperature excursion on a turbine**. Nine records (50%) carry vibration values at or above 7.0 mm/s \u2014 well into the ISO 10816 \"unsatisfactory/restricted operation\" band for most of these machine classes \u2014 while five units operate below 80% efficiency, which for rotating and heat-transfer equipment typically signals fouling, internal leakage, or hydraulic degradation.\n\nPriority ordering is as follows:\n\n| Priority | Unit / Record | Issue | Recommended Window |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| P1 | Turbine 2002 (0000007) | \u221215 \u00b0C inlet with low pressure | Immediate investigation |\n| P1 | Condensers 9813 (0000004) &",
